\f0\fs24 \cf0 Numerical Direct Scattering Transform for Dark Solitons\
\
This repository provides a numerical implementation of the direct scattering transform (DST) for dark solitons of the defocusing nonlinear Schr\'f6dinger equation (dNLSE) with continuous-wave (CW) boundary conditions.\
\
Reference: *I. Mullyadzhanov, S. Dremov, A. Gelash, "Numerical Direct Scattering Transform for Dark Solitons".\
\
Contents\
\
- DST_Functions.wl \'97 core Wolfram Mathematica package. Implements the Boffetta\'96Osborne transfer-matrix scheme adapted to CW boundary conditions; computes the scattering coefficient a(\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u955 )\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 , the norming constants \cf3 \cb4 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 \uc0\u961 \cf0 \cb1 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 , and auxiliary quantities needed for the discrete and continuous spectra.\
- SharingCode1S.nb \'97 example notebook for a single dark-soliton potential. Sets up the grid, CW background, potential, and boundary phases; visualizes \cf3 \cb4 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 \uc0\u968 \cf0 \cb1 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0  and the phase; demonstrates how to recover the soliton scattering data and compare with the analytical result.\
- SharingCodeRandom.nb \'97 example notebook for a random potential: two asymptotic plateaus with different phases, smooth tanh transitions, and a localized oscillatory perturbation. Includes generation of a randomly modulated hollow, computation of the asymptotic phases, and a root-finding procedure for the discrete eigenvalues and high-precision arithmetic.\
